 "remarks": "Historic New England charm meets modern-day living at 316 Chestnut Hill Road. Dating back to circa 1780, this beautifully updated 4-bedroom, 2.5-bath home is set on 1.5 picturesque acres in Norwalk's sought-after Cranbury neighborhood. Original wide-plank floors, exposed beams, two fireplaces, and beautiful stonework throughout the property showcase the home's character.  Thoughtfully updated for modern living, the home offers central air-a welcome luxury in a home of this vintage-along with a beautifully updated kitchen featuring high-end appliances and renovated baths. The first-floor primary suite is a standout, with vaulted ceilings and an en suite bath featuring a soaking tub. An attached two-car garage and whole-house generator provide additional comfort and convenience.  Outside, the property is made for entertaining. A swimming pool, screened porch, stone patio with built-in grill, and outdoor shower create a private backyard retreat. A charming barn adds even more potential-imagine a pool house, studio, home office, gym, or creative space.  Just down the street, enjoy access to the miles of wooded trails at beloved Cranbury Park, with Cranbury Shopping Center and Country Convenience nearby for shopping and dining. A special property that brings together nearly 250 years of history, beautiful grounds, modern updates, and an exceptional indoor-outdoor lifestyle.",
